process_dataset 08543c8aba0cb15c63ab22cedffd6202f8e254c16bb2d13f89fcf0fbb65b2df9 4771576d81b401b4124bc1caaa4ff06cdcb588b6487639471fd0e81d10f7f545 direction:P-0 PORTED 2026-10-08 (owner: "odmrazam, wariant D3") -- both engines now apply one divergence policy (snapsend.sh, snapget.sh): a backup landing follows its source and recv -F discards the surplus with a log line; sync and -t refuse. What still differs is direction: which side is remote, and snapget's guest_disk_is_live (snapget.sh), which reads guest state on the LOCAL node and has no remote twin in push. Also pull-only: the -M mirror's own plough label (snapget.sh, p0_what), since snapsend has no -M. W19 and W14 (2026-10-12, owner: "Odmrazaj") were ported to BOTH in one change: leaf_by_recv (-w or an encrypted parent, target_parent_encrypted) and the level-2 discard line for replica_-only snapshots (only_replica_snaps). W5 (2026-11-12) is pull-only: the --source-keep prune after a good pull (snapget.sh; REV-20261112-197, 2026-11-13: it now takes the target dataset and prunes only snapshots that target holds, still pull-only; round 2: the snapshot this run makes is stamped as the target's own, mark_source_owner called at snapget.sh; round 3: also for a successful quiesce window's snapshot, snapget.sh, pull-only; round 4 (F1d) was ported to BOTH: after a successful quiesce window the run copies exactly its own ${SNAP_MESSAGE}${RUN_SUFFIX} or refuses, snapget.sh, snapsend.sh); snapsend refuses the option (snapsend.sh) because the replica engine is snapget (gen-cron.sh replica_engine_cmd). Round 5 (F1e) was ported to BOTH: a quiesced member whose own snapshot is missing, -E-excluded or unreadable fails instead of passing as scaffolding, a resumed older stream no longer ends the member, and both local snapshot-only branches keep the window's snapshot.
